{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Who came to Egypt: seventy.</b> This means with Jacob, and the beginning of the matter proves this, as it is written ״אלה שמות״ etc. To inform that Jacob is part of the count with his sons, and he is included with the children of Leah, for in their enumeration there are only 32, and Scripture counts them as 33 with Jacob, because he is part of the first count, and from him it began to count the count of the seventy. And thus the plain sense of the verse: ״כל הנפש לבית יעקב הבאה מצרימה״ — if you wish to know their count, count with Jacob and you will find them seventy. And according to what I explained above, there is no need to say that Jacob is part of the count, for the Holy One, blessed be He, is counted with them and completes the count."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:10.268704606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}